- **src/context/contentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackContext`): Attachment point for Live Preview: this is the single React context that holds all CMS content and feeds every Contentstack component via useContent(). Live Preview data from Contentstack's real-time SDK must be injected here — the context value is what all components read from, so updating it with live preview payload instantly propagates to every consumer.
  - **Minimal fix:** Extend IContentstackContext to carry live preview state (e.g., a livePreviewData field or a content hash), and update the context provider (wherever it wraps the app) to subscribe to Contentstack Live Preview events and merge the incoming draft content into the existing context value so that useContent→getContentByKey returns the preview data instead of the published data. The existing useContent hook (src/hooks/useContent.ts) and getValue util (src/utils/getValue) need no changes — they already traverse whatever object the context holds.

## Reviewer Feedback — ADDRESS THESE (a prior code review requested changes)
The team-lead reviewer examined your previous attempt and requested the changes below. This is the highest priority: make the SMALLEST edits that resolve each point. If a point says the change is over-engineered or a more concise change/existing helper would do, REMOVE the excess and use the minimal approach — do not add more code.
- [blocker] The `onEntryChange` callback does `setValue((prev) => ({ ...prev }))` — a shallow copy of the same state with NO new data merged. The Contentstack Live Preview SDK's `onEntryChange` callback receives no arguments and does NOT mutate the context object in place (verified via resolve_package_symbol: `onEntryChange(callback: OnEntryChangeCallback)` — the callback signature takes no parameters). The comment claiming 'The SDK mutates the context object in place' is factually wrong. The prescribed root-cause fix requires merging incoming draft content into the context value so that `useContent→getContentByKey→getValue` returns preview data instead of published data. This callback is a no-op that triggers a re-render with identical values. None of the 5 verification criteria are met: changed entries do not update (VC1), unchanged entries trivially 'remain unchanged' because nothing changes (VC2), nav bar does not update (VC3), and disconnection/error resilience is moot since no data ever flows (VC5). (src/context/contentstackContext.tsx:60)
  - Suggested fix: Call the SDK's API inside the `onEntryChange` callback to fetch the updated entry data, then deep-merge that draft content into the context value at the correct path (e.g., `page[0]`). For example: `defaultExport.onEntryChange(() => { const updatedEntry = defaultExport.getEntryData?.() /* or whatever the SDK exposes */; setValue((prev) => ({ ...prev, page: [{ ...prev.page?.[0], ...updatedEntry }] })); });`. The merge must overlay draft fields onto the existing published content so `getValue(content, 'page.0.title')` returns the preview value.
