### What the previous summary got wrong

The conversation summary said "no `unsubscribe(uid)` exists" — that was incorrect. The static `ContentstackLivePreview.unsubscribeOnEntryChange` on the HOC class **does** take a `callbackUid` parameter (the return value of `onEntryChange`). Calling it with zero arguments fails typecheck (`TS2554`) and would fail at runtime. The correct fix uses the uid captured from `onEntryChange`.

Final implementation in the file:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (typeof window === "undefined") return;

  let callbackUid: string | undefined;
  try {
    callbackUid = ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange(() => {
      setValue((prev) => ({ ...prev }));
    });
  } catch (error) {
    // SDK may be unavailable outside a CMS preview session; fall back to published values.
    console.error(error);
  }

  return () => {
    if (callbackUid === undefined) return;
    try {
      ContentstackLivePreview.unsubscribeOnEntryChange(callbackUid);
    } catch {
      // best-effort cleanup on unmount
    }
  };
}, []);
```

